# QA macOS Release (Unsigned)

Use the **Build Without Notarize** workflow (`.github/workflows/build-without-notarize.yml`).

## Tag format

| Tag | Architecture | GitHub cache |
|-----|--------------|--------------|
| `mac-arm64-vX.Y.Z` | Apple Silicon | Yes |
| `mac-x64-vX.Y.Z` | Intel | Yes |
| `mac-arm64-no-cache-vX.Y.Z` | Apple Silicon | No — fresh downloads |
| `mac-x64-no-cache-vX.Y.Z` | Intel | No — fresh downloads |

## Release commands

Replace `0.0.1` with the QA version.

```bash
# Apple Silicon (cached binaries when possible)
git tag mac-arm64-v0.0.1
git push origin mac-arm64-v0.0.1

# Intel Macs (cached binaries when possible)
git tag mac-x64-v0.0.1
git push origin mac-x64-v0.0.1

# Force fresh binary downloads (skip GitHub Actions cache)
git tag mac-arm64-no-cache-v0.0.1
git push origin mac-arm64-no-cache-v0.0.1
```

Manual runs can also set **no_cache** in workflow_dispatch.

## After the workflow runs

1. Open the shared **Google Drive QA folder** (not GitHub Actions artifacts)
2. Download `mac-arm64-v0.0.1.zip` (or matching tag name)
3. Unzip → contains a `.dmg` or `.app`
4. Old `mac-*.zip` files are removed from Drive after **24 hours**
5. **Bypass Gatekeeper (Unsigned build):** macOS will say the app is "damaged" because it is unsigned. Open Terminal and run:
   ```bash
   xattr -cr /path/to/unzipped/OpenWhispr.app
   ```
   Then you can open it normally.

## Binary caching (GitHub Actions)

- **Prebuilt cache** (~400 MB/arch): whisper, llama, sherpa, qdrant, yt-dlp, meeting-aec, whisper-vad
- **Native cache**: compiled macOS helpers (globe, mic, audio-tap, etc.)
- **Electron cache**: separate, keyed on `pnpm-lock.yaml`
- Cache keys include pinned download versions (`scripts/ci-qa-cache-versions.js`)
- Free org limit: **10 GB cache per repo** (separate from the 500 MB artifact limit)
- `-no-cache` tags skip restore/save and pass `--force` to download scripts

## Secrets (`stage_env` environment)

- `GDRIVE_RCLONE_TOKEN` — Google Drive rclone OAuth token json
- `GDRIVE_CLIENT_ID` — Custom OAuth Client ID
- `GDRIVE_CLIENT_SECRET` — Custom OAuth Client Secret

## Notes

- Builds upload to **Google Drive**; the workflow deletes matching QA GitHub Actions artifacts afterward to save storage
